WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.167
Set up a crew: lead, size, hours, colour, members.

00:00:04.867 --> 00:00:07.633
New crew. Opens the crew form.

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:14.067
Crew name. What the schedule calls it, e.g. Hardscape 1. It must be filled in.

00:00:14.567 --> 00:00:26.400
Kind of work. hardscape, landscape, lighting… Won estimate sections from a matching catalogue category get this crew first. Customer notices in Settings go by it too.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:31.667
Crew lead. Who leads it (★). The lead is added to the members when you save.

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:35.600
People on the crew. How many usually work on it.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:46.267
Hours a day. Their working day. People × hours = the crew-hours a day; the schedule warns above it. The line under the colours works it out.

00:00:46.733 --> 00:00:56.633
Colour on the schedule. Each crew gets its own colour. A swatch with a dot is taken by another crew: pick one without a dot so crews look different.

00:00:57.133 --> 00:01:03.200
Any other colour. Or pick any colour here. If it looks like another crew's, a red line says so.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.400
Members. Tick everyone on the crew.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:12.133
Add crew. Saves the crew. People and hours a day must be above zero.

00:01:12.633 --> 00:01:16.367
Close the form. The tour closes it without saving.

00:01:16.867 --> 00:01:20.367
Change a crew. To change a crew, click its card.

00:01:20.867 --> 00:01:25.367
Active. Untick to take the crew off the schedule without deleting it.

00:01:25.867 --> 00:01:29.533
Save crew. Saves the changes and the member list.

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:33.233
Close it. The tour closes it without saving.

00:01:33.733 --> 00:01:39.333
That's it. You can play this tour in the app any time: press Help, and ask in your own words.
